    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d445">

                <pb facs="0635" n="521" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg521"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.51/1452: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The High Commissioner in Haiti</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Russell</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-12-01T14:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 1,
                                1922—2 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received December 2—10:40
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>150. My despatch number 85 of November 11th, 1922,<anchor n="69" xml:id="d445-f1"
                    /> and Department’s instruction number 53, November 13, 1922.<anchor n="69"
                        xml:id="d445-f2"/> In accordance with the Department’s instruction number
                    474 February 2, 1922<anchor n="70" xml:id="d445-f3"/> General Receiver has set
                    aside to [<hi rendition="#italic">the?</hi>] following amounts: Interest bank
                    note for the fiscal year 1921–22, $103,989.33; interest <pb facs="0636" n="522"
                        xml:id="pg522"/> guarantee National Railroad, $186,090.53; interest on the
                    interior debt, $111,929.59.</p>
                <p>The first item has been released by payments from the proceeds of the loan; the
                    last two items will become available as soon as the Financial Adviser will have
                    authorized payment from the proceeds of the loan. Authority is requested to
                    obtain the $300,000 mentioned,<anchor n="72" xml:id="d445-f4"/> first from funds
                    set aside for the service of old debts and now made available by the realization
                    of the loan; second from funds made available by the loan.</p>
                <p>Financial Adviser concurs. Funds much needed at this time for initial development
                    work.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Russell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
